 - [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
 - [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
 - [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a valid snapshot is imported, the system SHALL rebuild the SQLite index atomically and activate it only after the rebuild completes without exposing a partially rebuilt index.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When a lookup is performed against the active SQLite index, the system SHALL complete the lookup within 250 ms for 90,000 records on a kiosk with 4 GB of RAM.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When the snapshot schema version changes, the system SHALL rebuild the SQLite index using the new schema before activating the snapshot.
